  "question": {
    "text": "Let the maximum and minimum values of $\\left(\\sqrt{8 x-x^2-12}-4\\right)^2+(x-7)^2, x \\in \\mathbf{R}$ be $\\mathrm{M}$ and $\\mathrm{m}$, respectively. Then $\\mathrm{M}^2-\\mathrm{m}^2$ is equal to _________"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1600",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & (x-7)^2+(y-4)^2 \\\\ & y=\\sqrt{8 x-x^2-12} \\\\ & y^2=-(x-4)^2+16-12 \\\\ & (x-4)^2+y^2=4\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"assets\\st0028_1ba23e02d32d.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned} & m=9 \\\\ & M=41 \\\\ & M^2-m^2=41^2-9^2=1600\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}